usage assessment for xadmin/master/GetTransactionDetails.php
Repository evidence shows the endpoint is in use, not dead code:
Four tracked call sites target this exact file: get_detail.php and get_detail_experiment.php (browser links), refunds.php (browser AJAX), and paypal_transactions.php (server-to-server cURL with return=1).
The hardcoded PayPal credentials are on a live path — one of two credential sets is always selected and interpolated into the SOAP RequesterCredentials header, with the certificate passed to cURL, whenever the endpoint executes.
paypal_transactions.php is a complete, maintained import (last modified 2024 for PHP 8.1 compatibility, earlier fix for duplicate transactions), writing to six operational tables.
No newer PayPal implementation in the repo supersedes this flow.
What I could not determine from the repository: whether the import is currently scheduled. No in-repo invoker exists for paypal_transactions.php — but cron entries, systemd timers, and Jenkins jobs live outside the repo, so absence there is not evidence of disuse.
Outstanding — needs runtime confirmation: count of Active pp_here_account rows; access-log hits on the endpoint in the last 12 months; any schedule invoking the importer.
